  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Justify any conclusions and/or assumptions made in the context of the problem.\n\nA company’s cost is modelled by the equation $C=45x+9250$, and their revenue is modelled by $R=70x$. Determine the company’s break-even point.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=370$, with $C=R=25900$.",
      "worked": "At break-even, revenue equals cost.\n$$\\begin{align*}70x&=45x+9250\\\\25x&=9250\\\\x&=370\\\\R&=70(370)\\\\R&=25900\\\\C&=45(370)+9250\\\\C&=25900\\end{align*}$$\nThe break-even point is $(370,25900)$, where neither a profit nor a loss is made.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 21
  },
